<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 27 February, from 380 to 1939.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thessaloniki.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">380 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,646 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edict of Thessalonica makes Nicene Christianity Rome's state faith</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperors <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a>, Gratian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-ii">Valentinian II</a> decreed that all subjects should follow the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a>. Other Christians were branded heretics.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/907">907 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,119 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abaoji becomes khagan of the Khitans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-liao">Abaoji</a>, the Khitan leader later known as Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Taizu</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a>, became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khitans">Khitans</a>. Breaking with the custom of rotating leadership, he proclaimed himself emperor in 916 and built a state combining steppe and Chinese institutions.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-liao">Emperor Taizu of Liao</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khitans">Khitans</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">Khagan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1594">1594 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">432 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry IV crowned King of France at Chartres</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A former Protestant who had converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a>, Henry was crowned at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chartres">Chartres</a> because <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reims">Reims</a> was held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a>. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-nantes">Edict of Nantes</a> in 1598 ended the Wars of Religion.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1617">1617 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">409 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sweden and Russia sign the Treaty of Stolbovo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-stolbovo">Treaty of Stolbovo</a> ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingrian-war">Ingrian War</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. Sweden returned Novgorod, which it had occupied, but kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingria">Ingria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kexholm">Kexholm</a>, cutting Russia off from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-stolbovo">Treaty of Stolbovo</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingrian-war">Ingrian War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1812">1812 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lord Byron's maiden speech defends the Luddites</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the House of Lords, the young poet spoke against the Frame-Breaking Bill, which made wrecking machinery a capital crime. He blamed the desperation of the weavers on poverty, but the bill passed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1900">1900 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">126 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Labour Representation Committee founded in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Trade unionists and socialist societies formed a committee to elect working-class MPs. Renamed the Labour Party in 1906, it formed governments from 1924 and created the NHS in 1948.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1933">1933 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fire destroys the Reichstag in Berlin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The German parliament building burned and a young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> communist, Marinus van der Lubbe, was arrested. Next day Hitler secured a decree suspending civil liberties, a key step to dictatorship.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain and France recognise Franco's government</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> fallen, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> recognised the Nationalist regime as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s government a month before the Civil War ended. Franco ruled Spain until his death in 1975.</p></div></li></ol>
